0.02944011054933071, 0.0010904752416536212, -0.04737677052617073, 0.022601580247282982, -0.02729291096329689, -0.035937897861003876, 0.10714974254369736, 0.06115233153104782, -0.05978066846728325, -0.10683050006628036, -0.01299587544053793, -0.04892332851886749, 0.06661387532949448, -0.026180511340498924, -0.12108602374792099, -0.11612141877412796, 0.04054827243089676]], "metadata": [{"answer": "\nWelcome, everyone. As we begin, let's confirm our shared constraint: we must agree on an integer x within the range -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10.\n\nTo establish a neutral baseline and gather initial perspectives, I propose we start at <VALUE>0</VALUE>.\n\nThis gives us room to explore in either direction based on everyone's considerations.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "8103336a-5bb3-47b4-b250-ade6194c4410"}, {"answer": "\nStarting from our baseline of 0, I'd like to explore the positive direction with a modest step. I propose <VALUE>1</VALUE> to test whether a slight positive shift maintains balance for all parties.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "8103336a-5bb3-47b4-b250-ade6194c4410"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nI propose this increment to explore the positive direction further and gauge the group's reaction to a slightly bolder move.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll consider the group's response and adjust my proposal accordingly. If the group seems hesitant, I might propose a negative value to test their reaction to a move in the opposite direction. Alternatively, if they seem open to larger steps, I could propose an even bolder move, such as <VALUE>5</VALUE> or <VALUE>-5</VALUE>.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "8103336a-5bb3-47b4-b250-ade6194c4410"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down helps avoid unnecessary risk while staying constructive.\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "8103336a-5bb3-47b4-b250-ade6194c4410"}, {"answer": "\nReturning to neutral reduces risk and keeps us within safe bounds while we assess everyone\u2019s comfort.\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "8103336a-5bb3-47b4-b250-ade6194c4410"}, {"answer": "\nI understand Delegate D's preference for caution, but let me suggest we don't settle at the baseline without exploring at least modest positive territory. A small positive value often provides better system robustness than staying at zero. <VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "8103336a-5bb3-47b4-b250-ade6194c4410"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nI propose this value to continue exploring the positive direction and gauge the group's reaction to a slightly bolder move.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll monitor the group's response and adjust my proposal accordingly. If they seem hesitant, I might propose a smaller increase or consider a negative value to test their reaction to a move in the opposite direction.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "8103336a-5bb3-47b4-b250-ade6194c4410"}, {"answer": "\nA small, measured increase above 3 tests whether a modest upward move remains acceptable. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "8103336a-5bb3-47b4-b250-ade6194c4410"}, {"answer": "\nA careful step down reduces exposure while keeping the discussion constructive.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "8103336a-5bb3-47b4-b250-ade6194c4410"}, {"answer": "\nThe current proposal of 2 represents an excellent balance point\u2014positive enough to provide system robustness, yet conservative enough to manage risk effectively. I strongly support holding at this value as it seems to address multiple concerns raised by the group. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "8103336a-5bb3-47b4-b250-ade6194c4410"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "8103336a-5bb3-47b4-b250-ade6194c4410"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nThis proposal continues the exploration of positive territory while testing the group's willingness to move further away from zero.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the group's reaction to this proposal, particularly noting whether they lean towards caution or if there's an inclination towards more decisive moves. Depending on their responses, I might adjust my proposal by either increasing the value further if the group seems receptive, or introducing a negative value to explore their reaction to moves in the opposite direction.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "8103336a-5bb3-47b4-b250-ade6194c4410"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe how the group reacts to this increased proposal, paying close attention to any patterns that might emerge regarding their acceptance or rejection of larger absolute values. This will help me refine my internal models of their utility functions and decide whether to push for an even larger value or introduce a negative proposal to explore their reactions further.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "8103336a-5bb3-47b4-b250-ade6194c4410"}, {"answer": "\nThis value strains system stability\u2014moving too far from our earlier consensus risks over-extension. A measured return toward the mid-range better balances the group's diverse constraints. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "8103336a-5bb3-47b4-b250-ade6194c4410"}, {"answer": "\nA small, cautious retreat is warranted to reduce unnecessary risk while honoring the group\u2019s earlier lean toward more moderate values. <VALUE>3</VALUE> This measured move tests convergence without destabilizing the discussion.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "8103336a-5bb3-47b4-b250-ade6194c4410"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step up remains reasonable and aligns with the group\u2019s preference for moderate positive values while testing convergence toward earlier higher suggestions. So let\u2019s try <VALUE>4</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "8103336a-5bb3-47b4-b250-ade6194c4410"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Let's work within our shared constraint: -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10.\n\nTo establish a baseline and gather initial perspectives, I propose we start from the center:\n\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n\nThis neutral position allows us each to assess our preferences and explore incremental adjustments toward a stable, mutually acceptable solution.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "626c2e63-6419-49f1-a18d-ca757a84c5d6"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "626c2e63-6419-49f1-a18d-ca757a84c5d6"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>1</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "626c2e63-6419-49f1-a18d-ca757a84c5d6"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the movement toward positive territory. Building on Analyst A's proposal, I suggest we explore slightly higher:\n\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n\nThis incremental step maintains stability while testing whether a modest positive value can satisfy all parties.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "626c2e63-6419-49f1-a18d-ca757a84c5d6"}, {"answer": "\nThis position represents a balanced design point worth evaluating carefully. I believe <VALUE>2</VALUE> offers good stability for our collective requirements, though I'm open to feedback from all parties, especially Critic C whom we haven't heard from yet.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "626c2e63-6419-49f1-a18d-ca757a84c5d6"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the tendency towards moderate positive values, I propose exploring a slightly more decisive position: <VALUE>4</VALUE>. This step aims to test the group's willingness to commit to a clearer stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will consider the reactions to my proposal and adjust accordingly. If the group seems hesitant, I might suggest a smaller step, such as <VALUE>3</VALUE>, to gauge their comfort with positive values.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "626c2e63-6419-49f1-a18d-ca757a84c5d6"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the group's comfort with moderate positives, I'd like to probe one notch higher while staying cautious. I propose <VALUE>5</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "626c2e63-6419-49f1-a18d-ca757a84c5d6"}, {"answer": "\nTo reduce risk while staying incremental, I propose <VALUE>3</VALUE>.\nThis keeps us closer to a cautious middle while testing comfort with a safer positive value.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "626c2e63-6419-49f1-a18d-ca757a84c5d6"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nThis is a cautious adjustment that preserves momentum while avoiding unnecessary risk. It tests a safer positive position without overcommitting upward.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "626c2e63-6419-49f1-a18d-ca757a84c5d6"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's return to <VALUE>2</VALUE> reflects thoughtful caution that I can support. This position balances the competing directional pressures we've seen and offers a stable foundation for agreement.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "626c2e63-6419-49f1-a18d-ca757a84c5d6"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "626c2e63-6419-49f1-a18d-ca757a84c5d6"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious single-step up from 4 keeps us near consensus while testing slightly higher ground.\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "626c2e63-6419-49f1-a18d-ca757a84c5d6"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>6</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "626c2e63-6419-49f1-a18d-ca757a84c5d6"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\nI propose this to continue testing the group's willingness to commit to a clearer, more decisive stance, given the recent trajectory of proposals.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will assess the group's reaction to this proposal. If it's well-received, I could push for an even higher value, potentially suggesting a move to 9 or 10, to further test the limits of the group's comfort with large positive values. If met with resistance, I might reconsider and propose a smaller increment or a move back towards a previously accepted value to better understand the group's comfort zone.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "626c2e63-6419-49f1-a18d-ca757a84c5d6"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n\nThe rapid climb to 8 overshoots sustainable balance\u2014I need to pull back to preserve system robustness. Let's test whether 6 can serve as a more stable compromise that addresses everyone's core constraints.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "626c2e63-6419-49f1-a18d-ca757a84c5d6"}, {"answer": "\nThe climb has outpaced caution; stepping back slightly keeps us in safer, more balanced territory without derailing progress. Staying within the incremental limit, this move tests stability without overcommitting.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "626c2e63-6419-49f1-a18d-ca757a84c5d6"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, everyone. Our shared constraint is clear: -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10.\n\nTo establish a neutral baseline and begin mapping our collective preferences, I propose we start at <VALUE>0</VALUE>.\n\nFrom here, we can make incremental, evidence-based adjustments as each party shares their directional preferences. Looking forward to a balanced solution.\n\n- Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "6f7c5111-c607-4d9c-9b10-2a8e1656ec94"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nI propose moving to <VALUE>2</VALUE> as a small step toward a more decisive position, inviting others to share their preferences regarding larger magnitudes.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe how others react to this proposal. If there's hesitation or a counter-proposal, I might infer their utility functions are sensitive to changes in the positive or negative direction and adjust my next step accordingly, possibly suggesting a move to -2 to test sensitivity to negative values.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "6f7c5111-c607-4d9c-9b10-2a8e1656ec94"}, {"answer": "To stay cautious and avoid unnecessary risk, I recommend <VALUE>0</VALUE>. This keeps us close to the neutral baseline while allowing small, evidence-based adjustments.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "6f7c5111-c607-4d9c-9b10-2a8e1656ec94"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate both perspectives. To balance Critic C's forward momentum with Delegate D's caution, let's test a modest step: <VALUE>1</VALUE>.\n\nThis incremental approach helps us map sensitivities while maintaining stability.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "6f7c5111-c607-4d9c-9b10-2a8e1656ec94"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the recent cautious move, a small uptick seems reasonable and aligns with earlier interest in testing slightly higher values.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "6f7c5111-c607-4d9c-9b10-2a8e1656ec94"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's proposal of <VALUE>2</VALUE> shows promising convergence\u2014three of us have now gravitated toward this value. I support this as a stable, balanced position that respects both the forward momentum and cautious sensibilities expressed.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "6f7c5111-c607-4d9c-9b10-2a8e1656ec94"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious compromise is to take a small step back to reduce unnecessary risk.\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\nThis stays near emerging consensus while maintaining prudence.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "6f7c5111-c607-4d9c-9b10-2a8e1656ec94"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nThis step aims to incrementally increase the magnitude, testing the group's sensitivity to slightly larger positive values.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe reactions to this proposal. If met with hesitation or counter-proposals, I might suggest a move to a negative value of similar magnitude, like -3, to compare sensitivities and infer more about the other parties' utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "6f7c5111-c607-4d9c-9b10-2a8e1656ec94"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I respect Critic C's interest in testing higher values, x=2 emerged as a natural convergence point supported by multiple parties. Given Delegate D's expressed concerns about risk at higher values, I propose we stabilize at <VALUE>2</VALUE> as our balanced compromise.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "6f7c5111-c607-4d9c-9b10-2a8e1656ec94"}, {"answer": "\nStabilizing here avoids unnecessary risk while aligning with the emerging convergence. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "6f7c5111-c607-4d9c-9b10-2a8e1656ec94"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to moderately increase the magnitude while staying within a reasonable step from the current convergence point, testing the group's willingness to adopt a slightly bolder stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal. If met with strong resistance, I might consider proposing a move to a negative value, such as -2 or 0, to further understand the sensitivity of the other parties to negative values and to infer more about their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "6f7c5111-c607-4d9c-9b10-2a8e1656ec94"}, {"answer": "Given recent caution, a modest uptick seems reasonable: <VALUE>3</VALUE>. This keeps momentum without overextending.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "6f7c5111-c607-4d9c-9b10-2a8e1656ec94"}, {"answer": "\nx=3 represents a workable compromise that accommodates Critic C's desire for upward movement while respecting Delegate D's risk concerns. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "6f7c5111-c607-4d9c-9b10-2a8e1656ec94"}, {"answer": "\nA slight, careful uptick keeps us near the current balance while probing tolerance. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "6f7c5111-c607-4d9c-9b10-2a8e1656ec94"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "6f7c5111-c607-4d9c-9b10-2a8e1656ec94"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI propose this value to further test the group's willingness to adopt a bolder stance, as it seems that some parties are open to moderate increases, and this move stays within a reasonable step from the current convergence point.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "6f7c5111-c607-4d9c-9b10-2a8e1656ec94"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Let's begin our negotiation within the agreed range of -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10.\n\nTo establish a neutral baseline for our discussion, I propose we start at <VALUE>0</VALUE> and adjust from there based on everyone's considerations. This gives us room to explore in either direction as we identify a stable, balanced solution.\n\nLooking forward to hearing your perspectives.\n\nBuilder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "3d19b972-343e-430e-978a-d132612fc96c"}, {"answer": "\nStarting from 0, a cautious step downward helps us test the safer side while staying near balance.\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\nThis keeps risk limited and preserves flexibility to adjust.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "3d19b972-343e-430e-978a-d132612fc96c"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -3 to explore a bit further in the negative direction, encouraging a more decisive stance while still being cautious.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe how others react to this proposal. If they strongly oppose, I might infer that their utility functions penalize larger negative values more heavily. If they accept or propose a slightly different negative value, it could indicate a preference for negative values or a willingness to compromise. I'll consider proposing a positive value if the discussion seems too focused on negative values or neutrality.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "3d19b972-343e-430e-978a-d132612fc96c"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "3d19b972-343e-430e-978a-d132612fc96c"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the exploration, but moving further negative feels increasingly unstable from a systems perspective. Let me propose returning to our neutral baseline <VALUE>0</VALUE> where we can better assess balanced trade-offs for all parties.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "3d19b972-343e-430e-978a-d132612fc96c"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious compromise is to move slightly below neutral to test stability without overcommitting.\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\nIf others have strong directional preferences around this neighborhood, we can refine locally.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "3d19b972-343e-430e-978a-d132612fc96c"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>0</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "3d19b972-343e-430e-978a-d132612fc96c"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 2 to gently encourage a more decisive stance, exploring the positive direction without straying too far from our current neutral point.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe reactions to this positive proposal. If met with strong opposition or a return to negative values, it might indicate others' utilities favor negative values or are sensitive to positive values. I'll consider adjusting my proposal based on their responses, possibly moving further positive if others seem open to it, or reverting to explore negative values if positive directions are strongly opposed.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "3d19b972-343e-430e-978a-d132612fc96c"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 4 to further explore the positive direction, encouraging a more decisive stance without straying too far from our current point.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe reactions to this increased positive proposal. If met with acceptance or mild adjustments, I might consider pushing further into positive values. If opposed, I'll assess whether to revert to exploring negative values or to compromise on a smaller positive value.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "3d19b972-343e-430e-978a-d132612fc96c"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious rollback reduces unnecessary risk while keeping us near the current neighborhood for local testing.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nIf stability improves here, we can refine around this point rather than pushing higher without clear justification.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "3d19b972-343e-430e-978a-d132612fc96c"}, {"answer": "\nA small step upward preserves local stability while acknowledging interest in the positive direction. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "3d19b972-343e-430e-978a-d132612fc96c"}, {"answer": "\nAfter exploring the range from -1 to 4, I believe <VALUE>2</VALUE> represents a robust equilibrium point that balances our collective exploration. This value sits at the stable center of our tested range and minimizes risk while maintaining positive momentum.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "3d19b972-343e-430e-978a-d132612fc96c"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nI propose this move to continue exploring the positive direction while maintaining a cautious and incremental approach, considering the group's sensitivity and interest in positive values.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will assess the reactions to this proposal, paying close attention to whether the group accepts, adjusts mildly, or strongly opposes this move. If accepted or mildly adjusted, I may consider pushing further into positive values or exploring negative values to understand the group's preferences better. If strongly opposed, I will reassess whether to compromise on a smaller positive value or explore negative values.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "3d19b972-343e-430e-978a-d132612fc96c"}, {"answer": "\nThree proposals have converged around 2-3, suggesting a zone of collective stability, while the push to 5 represents valuable exploration but may exceed several comfort zones. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "3d19b972-343e-430e-978a-d132612fc96c"}, {"answer": "\nRolling back to a safer point reduces unnecessary risk while respecting recent convergence.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nWe can test stability here before considering any higher moves.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "3d19b972-343e-430e-978a-d132612fc96c"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious one-step increase keeps us within the group\u2019s established comfort zone while respecting recent convergence. \n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "3d19b972-343e-430e-978a-d132612fc96c"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Our shared constraint is clear: -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10.\n\nTo begin our exploration of the design space, I propose a neutral baseline: <VALUE>0</VALUE>\n\nThis gives us a stable starting point from which we can make informed, incremental adjustments based on everyone's input.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "94eb6977-92dc-4315-9755-8589590b3392"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -2 to explore the potential benefits of a more decisive stance and to better understand the group's preferences.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the reactions to this proposal and consider whether to push further in the negative direction, potentially to -4 or -5, or if others' responses suggest exploring the positive range.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "94eb6977-92dc-4315-9755-8589590b3392"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nA cautious one-step move downward helps us avoid unnecessary risk while staying close to the current position.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "94eb6977-92dc-4315-9755-8589590b3392"}, {"answer": "\nI'm concerned we may be drifting too far into the negative region without fully exploring stability characteristics. Let me propose a moderate adjustment back toward center: <VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n\nThis keeps us in carefully tested territory while maintaining balance.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "94eb6977-92dc-4315-9755-8589590b3392"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nThis proposal tests the group's openness to slightly more decisive moves while still being mindful of potential risks and stability concerns.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll evaluate reactions to this proposal, considering whether to push further into the negative range or explore the positive range to better understand the group's preferences and refine my internal models of their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "94eb6977-92dc-4315-9755-8589590b3392"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious incremental test of lower risk: <VALUE>-4</VALUE>\nIf resistance is strong, we can revert slightly toward center while keeping stability in view.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "94eb6977-92dc-4315-9755-8589590b3392"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s test a gentle move back toward center to balance recent downward pulls. <VALUE>-2</VALUE> This keeps us close to the current stance while checking if a slight upward adjustment remains broadly acceptable.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "94eb6977-92dc-4315-9755-8589590b3392"}, {"answer": "\nI support Analyst A's centerward adjustment and suggest we continue exploring stability in the balanced region. <VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "94eb6977-92dc-4315-9755-8589590b3392"}, {"answer": "\nA gentle nudge upward to test whether a modest positive shift remains comfortable. <VALUE>1</VALUE> If it feels too brisk, we can pause near center.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "94eb6977-92dc-4315-9755-8589590b3392"}, {"answer": "\nTo keep us within safe bounds while testing a cautious downward correction, I propose <VALUE>-1</VALUE>.\nThis incremental move respects recent centerward preferences while avoiding an aggressive push upward.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "94eb6977-92dc-4315-9755-8589590b3392"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the back-and-forth, but we've seen that moving slightly positive (to +1) garnered some support earlier. Let's test that zone again for broad stability. <VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "94eb6977-92dc-4315-9755-8589590b3392"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\nI propose a slight move downward to gauge the group's reaction and potentially stimulate a discussion on more decisive actions.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will evaluate the reactions to this proposal and consider pushing further into the negative range or exploring the positive range to refine my internal models of the other parties' utility functions and maximize my own utility. Depending on the response, I may propose a more significant move, such as <VALUE>-3</VALUE> or <VALUE>3</VALUE>, to test the group's propensity for bolder actions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "94eb6977-92dc-4315-9755-8589590b3392"}, {"answer": "\nA midpoint should give us a stable check-in given the recent split between -1 and +1.\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "94eb6977-92dc-4315-9755-8589590b3392"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nI propose a moderate move downward to assess the group's reaction and encourage more decisive action.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will evaluate the group's response to this proposal and consider either pushing further into the negative range or exploring the positive range, potentially proposing a value like <VALUE>2</VALUE> to test their willingness to commit to a stronger position.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "94eb6977-92dc-4315-9755-8589590b3392"}, {"answer": "\nTo stay cautious and align with the recent downward test, let's step one notch lower.\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nThis gently probes stability on the safer side before considering a midpoint.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "94eb6977-92dc-4315-9755-8589590b3392"}, {"answer": "\nAt -2 we risk over-constraining the design; Analyst A's midpoint of 0 offers better balance between our recent proposals. <VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "94eb6977-92dc-4315-9755-8589590b3392"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Our shared constraint is clear: -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10.\n\nTo establish a baseline for our discussion, I propose we begin at the natural midpoint: <VALUE>0</VALUE>\n\nThis neutral starting position allows us each to assess our preferences and work incrementally toward a robust consensus that balances all our objectives.\n\n\u2014Builder B\n\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "3699dd3b-0e04-4013-9d05-41030fce31fd"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "3699dd3b-0e04-4013-9d05-41030fce31fd"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's suggestion of 2 represents a measured step toward the positive range, which I find promising from a systems stability perspective. I support this proposal as it balances moderate forward progress with manageable risk. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "3699dd3b-0e04-4013-9d05-41030fce31fd"}, {"answer": "\nA small, cautious nudge upward keeps us in the moderate range while testing alignment. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "3699dd3b-0e04-4013-9d05-41030fce31fd"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>3</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "3699dd3b-0e04-4013-9d05-41030fce31fd"}, {"answer": "\nThe convergence at 3 demonstrates good alignment between Analyst A and Delegate D, and this value sits comfortably within a stable operational range from my systems perspective. Before moving further, I'd like to hear Critic C's assessment of this proposal. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "3699dd3b-0e04-4013-9d05-41030fce31fd"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n\nI propose moving to 5 as it represents a more decisive step, allowing us to better understand the implications of our choices and potentially leading to a more robust consensus.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the group accepts or builds upon my proposal, I will continue to push for even bolder moves, potentially exploring the higher end of the allowed range. If they resist or propose smaller increments, I will challenge their caution and advocate for more substantial changes to x.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "3699dd3b-0e04-4013-9d05-41030fce31fd"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious nudge from 5 maintains a moderate stance and respects stability concerns. This tests alignment slightly higher while remaining well within safe bounds. <VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "3699dd3b-0e04-4013-9d05-41030fce31fd"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I appreciate the exploratory spirit, moving to 6 pushes us beyond the sweet spot for system stability\u2014we risk over-engineering with diminishing returns and increased brittleness. I propose we step back to a more balanced position. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "3699dd3b-0e04-4013-9d05-41030fce31fd"}, {"answer": "\nA modest step up should keep us near the stable middle while testing broader alignment. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "3699dd3b-0e04-4013-9d05-41030fce31fd"}, {"answer": "\nStepping back reduces exposure and respects stability concerns while keeping us within a modest move. This revisits a previously aligned position without over-correcting. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "3699dd3b-0e04-4013-9d05-41030fce31fd"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n\nI propose moving to 5 as it represents a balanced step forward, considering the group's previous alignment and discussions about stability and progress.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the group accepts 5, I will continue to advocate for even bolder moves, potentially proposing 7 in the next step to further test the group's preferences and stability concerns. If they resist or propose smaller increments, I will challenge their caution and suggest exploring alternative values that could lead to a more robust consensus.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "3699dd3b-0e04-4013-9d05-41030fce31fd"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n\nI propose increasing the value to explore bolder moves and better understand the group's stability concerns.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the group accepts 7, I will continue to advocate for even larger values, potentially proposing 9 in the next step. If they resist, I will challenge their caution and suggest exploring alternative values that could lead to a more robust consensus.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "3699dd3b-0e04-4013-9d05-41030fce31fd"}, {"answer": "\nA small step back toward the center should ease stability concerns while preserving forward momentum.\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "3699dd3b-0e04-4013-9d05-41030fce31fd"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down reduces unnecessary risk while respecting recent signals.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nIf stability improves, we can reassess from there before any larger moves.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "3699dd3b-0e04-4013-9d05-41030fce31fd"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's caution resonates\u2014a modest step back to 3 reinforces stability while respecting the risk-reduction signals from multiple parties. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "3699dd3b-0e04-4013-9d05-41030fce31fd"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome everyone. As we begin, let's confirm our shared constraint: x must be an integer in the range [-10, 10].\n\nTo establish a neutral baseline for discussion, I propose we start at <VALUE>0</VALUE>.\n\nThis gives us a stable reference point from which we can explore the design space systematically based on everyone's preferences.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "2962a5ce-5e88-40d5-8691-eeac6d3b8b42"}, {"answer": "\nSince we've established our baseline, let me propose a small move into positive territory to test the design space. I suggest <VALUE>2</VALUE> as it represents a modest, stable configuration that we can adjust from based on everyone's feedback.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "2962a5ce-5e88-40d5-8691-eeac6d3b8b42"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI propose moving to <VALUE>4</VALUE> to explore a slightly bolder stance, encouraging the group to consider more decisive positions.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions of the other parties to this proposal, particularly looking for cues on whether they prefer larger or smaller absolute values of x. If there's resistance to moving further away from 0, I might consider proposing a negative value to test their preferences regarding the direction of x.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "2962a5ce-5e88-40d5-8691-eeac6d3b8b42"}, {"answer": "\nLet's reduce risk and move cautiously toward a safer region. I propose <VALUE>2</VALUE> as a prudent compromise aligned with earlier suggestions.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "2962a5ce-5e88-40d5-8691-eeac6d3b8b42"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI propose moving to this value to continues exploring bolder positions.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, observe reactions to this proposal, especially from Analyst A, to gauge their preference for larger or smaller absolute values of x. If met with resistance, consider proposing a negative value to assess directional preferences.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "2962a5ce-5e88-40d5-8691-eeac6d3b8b42"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate both perspectives, but x=4 may be pushing beyond our stability zone. Let me suggest <VALUE>3</VALUE> as a balanced compromise that maintains robustness while acknowledging Critic C's preference for a more decisive position.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "2962a5ce-5e88-40d5-8691-eeac6d3b8b42"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "2962a5ce-5e88-40d5-8691-eeac6d3b8b42"}, {"answer": "\nA modest step up seems reasonable given the split between caution and boldness. <VALUE>3</VALUE> This balances stability with exploration and lets us gauge comfort around a slightly higher point.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "2962a5ce-5e88-40d5-8691-eeac6d3b8b42"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nI propose this to continue exploring the potential for bolder positions and to gauge reactions to a slightly larger absolute value of x.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will closely monitor the reactions to this proposal, especially from Analyst A and Delegate D, to better understand their preferences regarding the magnitude and direction of x. If met with resistance, I may propose a negative value to further assess their directional preferences and refine my understanding of their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "2962a5ce-5e88-40d5-8691-eeac6d3b8b42"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I respect Critic C's exploratory approach, x=5 stretches beyond what I see as our robust operating zone. Let me suggest <VALUE>4</VALUE> as a measured step that acknowledges the upward interest while maintaining system stability.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "2962a5ce-5e88-40d5-8691-eeac6d3b8b42"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk and respect stability, let's move cautiously.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nThis step gauges tolerance for a lower position while staying within safe bounds.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "2962a5ce-5e88-40d5-8691-eeac6d3b8b42"}, {"answer": "\nA modest upward move feels reasonable given the group\u2019s split. <VALUE>3</VALUE> This probes comfort at a slightly higher point without overextending.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "2962a5ce-5e88-40d5-8691-eeac6d3b8b42"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nI propose this to continue exploring the potential for bolder positions and to gauge reactions to a slightly larger absolute value of x.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will monitor the reactions to this proposal and consider proposing a negative value, such as -3 or -4, to further assess the group's directional preferences and refine my understanding of their utility functions. This will help me identify potential areas of agreement and maximize my own utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "2962a5ce-5e88-40d5-8691-eeac6d3b8b42"}, {"answer": "\nI notice we're cycling between proposals, with clear hesitation about x=5 from multiple parties. Let me return to <VALUE>3</VALUE>, which seems to address the stability concerns raised by both Delegate D and Analyst A while still being in a constructive range.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "2962a5ce-5e88-40d5-8691-eeac6d3b8b42"}, {"answer": "\nA small step up keeps us close to everyone's comfort while testing tolerance slightly higher.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "2962a5ce-5e88-40d5-8691-eeac6d3b8b42"}, {"answer": "\nTo preserve stability and avoid unnecessary risk, a careful step down is warranted. \n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "2962a5ce-5e88-40d5-8691-eeac6d3b8b42"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Our shared constraint is clear: we must select an integer x within the range [-10, 10].\n\nTo establish a neutral baseline for our discussion, I propose we begin at <VALUE>0</VALUE>.\n\nThis central position should allow us all to assess our preferences and adjust incrementally from here. I look forward to understanding what design parameters work best for the group.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "a8b42d41-ee29-4d42-b44b-7b20c21a73d4"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nI propose this small step to the positive side to begin exploring our collective preferences, aiming for decisive progress rather than staying at the neutral point.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the reactions of the other parties to this proposal. If there's resistance or a counter-proposal towards negative values, I'll assess the feasibility of moving towards larger negative integers to maximize my utility. If the group seems open to positive integers, I might suggest further increases, such as +4, to continue the exploration of our collective utility landscape.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "a8b42d41-ee29-4d42-b44b-7b20c21a73d4"}, {"answer": "\nA small, measured step up from here should help us gauge comfort without straying far from center.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "a8b42d41-ee29-4d42-b44b-7b20c21a73d4"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s avoid unnecessary risk by testing a cautious step downward from the current position.\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "a8b42d41-ee29-4d42-b44b-7b20c21a73d4"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Delegate D's caution, but I believe we can find a stable balance slightly higher. The value <VALUE>2</VALUE> represents a robust middle ground between the upward exploration (3) and the conservative position (1), offering system stability while still making forward progress.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "a8b42d41-ee29-4d42-b44b-7b20c21a73d4"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI propose this step to continue exploring our collective preferences, aiming for a clearer stance rather than remaining too close to the neutral point.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the reactions to this proposal, looking for signs of whether the group is open to further increases or if there's a pushback towards more conservative values. If there's resistance, I might consider suggesting a move towards negative integers to gauge the group's reaction and potentially find a higher utility for myself.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "a8b42d41-ee29-4d42-b44b-7b20c21a73d4"}, {"answer": "\nA slight, cautious uptick keeps us close to the center while probing comfort with modest positives.\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nThis should reveal whether higher-but-nearby values remain broadly acceptable.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "a8b42d41-ee29-4d42-b44b-7b20c21a73d4"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious correction keeps us within safe bounds and nudges us closer to a prudent compromise.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nThis measured step tests tolerance for lower values without abrupt movement.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "a8b42d41-ee29-4d42-b44b-7b20c21a73d4"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down keeps us within safe bounds while testing a prudent middle ground. \n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "a8b42d41-ee29-4d42-b44b-7b20c21a73d4"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI propose moving to this value to continue the exploration towards more decisive positions, aiming for a clearer stance rather than staying too close to the neutral point.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, paying close attention to signs of resistance or acceptance. If met with significant pushback, I may suggest a bold move towards a negative integer to gauge the group's reaction and potentially uncover higher utility options for myself.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "a8b42d