gently testing higher positives.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nThis compromise respects stability and maintains momentum without overshooting.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "a8b42d41-ee29-4d42-b44b-7b20c21a73d4"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Our shared constraint is clear: -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10.\n\nTo establish a neutral baseline for our discussion, I propose we start at <VALUE>0</VALUE> and adjust from there based on everyone's perspectives. This gives us room to move in either direction as we learn what works best for the group.\n\nLooking forward to a balanced solution.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "a045c0bc-fd90-4805-923a-48e1c6387843"}, {"answer": "\nA small step up from the neutral baseline seems reasonable to test comfort in the positive direction while staying close to center.\nThis keeps flexibility if others prefer moderation.\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "a045c0bc-fd90-4805-923a-48e1c6387843"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's suggestion to explore the positive direction makes sense for testing stability. Moving incrementally to <VALUE>2</VALUE> continues this measured approach while we gather more information about what works for everyone.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "a045c0bc-fd90-4805-923a-48e1c6387843"}, {"answer": "To avoid unnecessary risk and stay within safe bounds, I recommend a small step back from 2. I propose <VALUE>1</VALUE>.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "a045c0bc-fd90-4805-923a-48e1c6387843"}, {"answer": "\nI hear Delegate D's caution about risk, and it's a valid perspective. However, <VALUE>2</VALUE> still represents a modest, stable position that balances exploration with safety\u2014I'd like to hear from Critic C before we settle.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "a045c0bc-fd90-4805-923a-48e1c6387843"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious nudge upward from 2 can 