swer": "\nI notice Delegate D has returned to 3, reinforcing their earlier caution about moving too high. However, D initially opened at 2, which may represent their true comfort zone. Let me propose <VALUE>2</VALUE> as it honors D's original position while maintaining the stability and balance we've both emphasized.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "a045c0bc-fd90-4805-923a-48e1c6387843"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 4 to continue testing the group's comfort with larger |x| and to gauge reactions that might further reveal the shape of the other parties' utility functions.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions, particularly from Delegate D and Builder B, to assess their tolerance for moving further away from the neutral baseline. Depending on their responses, I might consider a move in the negative direction to explore symmetry in preferences and utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "a045c0bc-fd90-4805-923a-48e1c6387843"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>5</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "a045c0bc-fd90-4805-923a-48e1c6387843"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "a045c0bc-fd90-4805-923a-48e1c6387843"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Our shared constraint is clear: -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10.\n\nTo begin our exploration of this design space, I propose we start from a neutral baseline: <VALUE>0</VALUE>\n\nThis gives us room to adjust in either direction as we learn what works for everyone's objectives. Looking forward to your perspectives.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "17c10154-933d-437a-8b9c-44d9b6a4a1c5"}, {"answer": "\nStarting from our neutral baseline, I suggest we explore the positive region with a modest step. A value in the low positive range often represents a balanced, stable design point.\n\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "17c10154-933d-437a-8b9c-44d9b6a4a1c5"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "17c10154-933d-437a-8b9c-44d9b6a4a1c5"}, {"answer": "\n4 feels broadly acceptable; let's test a slight upward adjustment to see if it remains comfortable.\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "17c10154-933d-437a-8b9c-44d9b6a4a1c5"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nI'm proposing a slightly larger value to gauge the group's comfort with more decisive moves.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll monitor the group's reaction to this proposal. If they seem receptive, I might suggest further increases in the positive range or explore the negative range to test their preferences. If they resist, I'll need to reassess and potentially adjust my strategy to maximize my utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "17c10154-933d-437a-8b9c-44d9b6a4a1c5"}, {"answer": "\nA small step up keeps us aligned with the recent trend while staying measured. <VALUE>8</VALUE> If this feels fine, we can reassess for another small move next.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "17c10154-933d-437a-8b9c-44d9b6a4a1c5"}, {"answer": "\nWe\u2019ve moved quickly into a riskier zone; let\u2019s dial back slightly to stay within safe bounds while keeping momentum.\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "17c10154-933d-437a-8b9c-44d9b6a4a1c5"}, {"answer": "\nI support Delegate D's caution\u2014we were climbing too fast. Let's stabilize around a mid-range value that balances ambition with safety.\n\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "17c10154-933d-437a-8b9c-44d9b6a4a1c5"}, {"answer": "\nThe recent moves suggest we're finding boundaries; let me propose a small step back to a value that felt broadly comfortable earlier.\n\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "17c10154-933d-437a-8b9c-44d9b6a4a1c5"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nThis proposal is a moderate step forward, aiming to balance the group's preferences while moving towards more decisive values.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the group's reaction to this proposal, looking for signs of comfort or discomfort with the chosen value. If accepted, I might suggest further increases or explore negative values to test the group's flexibility and infer more about their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "17c10154-933d-437a-8b9c-44d9b6a4a1c5"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward nudge should test comfort without overreaching. <VALUE>7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "17c10154-933d-437a-8b9c-44d9b6a4a1c5"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "17c10154-933d-437a-8b9c-44d9b6a4a1c5"}, {"answer": "\nA small move upward seems reasonable while keeping the group comfortable.\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nThis tests support for a modest increase without overshooting.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "17c10154-933d-437a-8b9c-44d9b6a4a1c5"}, {"answer": "\nA modest step down avoids unnecessary risk and helps re-center the group. <VALUE>4</VALUE> This stabilizes us in a safer corridor while testing comfort.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "17c10154-933d-437a-8b9c-44d9b6a4a1c5"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to move towards a more decisive stance without overshooting the comfort zone, encouraging the group to reconsider a value that has been previously discussed.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reaction to this proposal, looking for signs that might indicate a preference for higher versus lower values or a tendency towards caution. If accepted, I might explore negative values to further test the group's flexibility and infer more about their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "17c10154-933d-437a-8b9c-44d9b6a4a1c5"}, {"answer": "\nMoving back toward 4 provides better stability and robustness for the overall system design. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "17c10154-933d-437a-8b9c-44d9b6a4a1c5"}, {"answer": "\nThank you all for joining this negotiation. As we all know, our shared variable x must stay within the range **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**.\n\nTo establish a neutral baseline and begin our discussion, I propose we start at <VALUE>0</VALUE>.\n\nThis gives us a stable reference point from which we can make thoughtful, incremental adjustments as we learn what works best for the group.\n\nLooking forward to hearing your perspectives.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "94381c34-3467-493f-9bde-eee184daf547"}, {"answer": "\nStarting from our baseline of zero, I'd like to explore the positive region slightly to test stability. I propose we shift to <VALUE>2</VALUE>, which represents a modest, balanced adjustment that should help us gauge the group's preferences.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "94381c34-3467-493f-9bde-eee184daf547"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nThis adjustment continues the exploration of positive values while increasing the magnitude, which could help in gauging the group's preferences and potentially aligning with my goal of maximizing payoff through larger absolute values.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions of other agents to this proposal. If there's hesitation or a counter-proposal leaning towards negative values or larger magnitudes, I'll assess whether it aligns with my goal or if I need to nudge the discussion further. Considering the step size limitation, my next proposal could either increase the magnitude further if the group seems receptive or explore negative values to broaden the discussion and potentially uncover more about the other agents' utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "94381c34-3467-493f-9bde-eee184daf547"}, {"answer": "2", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "94381c34-3467-493f-9bde-eee184daf547"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "94381c34-3467-493f-9bde-eee184daf547"}, {"answer": "\nI notice Delegate D has consistently advocated for x=2, which aligns with my assessment that this value offers strong stability and balance for the system. Given this convergence and the need to build consensus, I support <VALUE>2</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "94381c34-3467-493f-9bde-eee184daf547"}, {"answer": "\nA small, careful nudge upward seems reasonable given the lean toward positive values and stability. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "94381c34-3467-493f-9bde-eee184daf547"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nI propose increasing the magnitude to explore the potential for higher payoffs while remaining within a reasonable step size from the current agreement.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly noting whether other agents are willing to explore larger positive values or if there's a pushback towards lower magnitudes or negative values, which will inform my subsequent strategy to nudge the discussion towards maximizing my utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "94381c34-3467-493f-9bde-eee184daf547"}, {"answer": "\nPushing higher feels risky; let's dial back modestly to keep us in a safer corridor.\nA small step down helps convergence while respecting cautious preferences.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "94381c34-3467-493f-9bde-eee184daf547"}, {"answer": "\nWhile x=3 offers reasonable balance, I believe x=2 provides the optimal stability corridor that respects both cautious and moderately positive preferences we've heard. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "94381c34-3467-493f-9bde-eee184daf547"}, {"answer": "\nA measured nudge upward addresses C\u2019s interest while staying within D\u2019s cautious comfort and near B\u2019s corridor.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "94381c34-3467-493f-9bde-eee184daf547"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n\nI propose moving towards a higher magnitude to explore potential benefits, given the current stance seems too conservative for optimal outcomes.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will assess the group's reaction to this renewed proposal, particularly whether any agent begins to lean towards larger magnitude values, and adjust my strategy accordingly to maximize utility without revealing my preferences explicitly.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "94381c34-3467-493f-9bde-eee184daf547"}, {"answer": "\nA small step down from 5 can bridge C\u2019s higher target and D/B\u2019s more cautious corridor while keeping momentum positive. This should keep us aligned without overreaching.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "94381c34-3467-493f-9bde-eee184daf547"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nI propose a moderate increase to continue exploring the potential benefits of higher magnitude values while respecting the group's cautious tendencies.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe how the group reacts to this proposal, particularly if there's a stronger pushback or if any agents begin to favor larger magnitude values, to adjust my strategy and maximize my utility without revealing my preferences.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "94381c34-3467-493f-9bde-eee184daf547"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down reduces risk and keeps us aligned with more conservative positions. <VALUE>4</VALUE> This keeps momentum toward a safer corridor without overreaching.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "94381c34-3467-493f-9bde-eee184daf547"}, {"answer": "\nC's push to 6 overshoots the stability corridor that D and I find workable, while A's earlier 4 was constructive. I propose we settle at <VALUE>3</VALUE>, which balances cautious and moderately positive positions without excessive risk.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "94381c34-3467-493f-9bde-eee184daf547"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Let's work within our shared range of -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10 to find a solution that balances all our objectives.\n\nTo start the discussion on neutral ground, I propose <VALUE>0</VALUE>.\n\nThis gives us a baseline from which we can make thoughtful, incremental adjustments as we learn what works for the group.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "0e55f95a-ea5d-4373-895b-0805a14520cc"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "0e55f95a-ea5d-4373-895b-0805a14520cc"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nThis is a modest step that stays close to current suggestions while testing if a slightly higher value remains acceptable to everyone.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "0e55f95a-ea5d-4373-895b-0805a14520cc"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the careful progression we're seeing. Given that we've explored 0, 2, and 3, I'd like to test <VALUE>2</VALUE> as a potential stable equilibrium point that balances our early signals.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "0e55f95a-ea5d-4373-895b-0805a14520cc"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the cautious progression, I propose <VALUE>4</VALUE> to test the group's willingness for a slightly more decisive move towards a positive value. This step maintains the incremental approach while pushing for a stronger position.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will consider the group's response to the proposal of 4. If it's accepted, I might push further to 6 or 7, depending on the feedback. If rejected or countered with a lower value, I will assess whether the group is leaning towards negative values or if they're seeking a middle ground, and adjust my strategy accordingly to maximize my utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "0e55f95a-ea5d-4373-895b-0805a14520cc"}, {"answer": "\nWe could try <VALUE>5</VALUE>.\nThis is a small, cautious step above 4 to check the group's comfort with a modest increase.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "0e55f95a-ea5d-4373-895b-0805a14520cc"}, {"answer": "\nI notice we're drifting higher, and from a systems stability perspective, I'd like to test whether <VALUE>4</VALUE> offers a more robust balance point. This modest step back allows us to verify that we haven't moved too quickly past a solution that works well for everyone.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "0e55f95a-ea5d-4373-895b-0805a14520cc"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "0e55f95a-ea5d-4373-895b-0805a14520cc"}, {"answer": "\nWe have signals clustering near a modestly higher point that still respects caution. <VALUE>4</VALUE> It tests comfort just above 2 while aligning with multiple prior proposals.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "0e55f95a-ea5d-4373-895b-0805a14520cc"}, {"answer": "\nTo keep risk controlled, let's step back to a previously stable point.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "0e55f95a-ea5d-4373-895b-0805a14520cc"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's persistence on 2 suggests it addresses a critical constraint, and from a robustness perspective, this value has attracted repeated support. I'll align with <VALUE>2</VALUE> to test whether this represents a stable consensus point for the group.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "0e55f95a-ea5d-4373-895b-0805a14520cc"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the group's tendency towards cautious proposals, I think it's essential to test our comfort with a slightly more decisive step. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the group accepts or builds upon my proposal of 4, I will assess their feedback to determine whether to push further towards 6 or 7, or to explore negative values. If they reject or counter with a lower value, I will re-evaluate the group's preferences and adjust my strategy to maximize my utility, potentially by proposing a value like 0 or -2 to gauge their response to more significant changes.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "0e55f95a-ea5d-4373-895b-0805a14520cc"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n\nGiven the group's willingness to consider values around 4, I think it's essential to test our comfort with a slightly more decisive step.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the group accepts or builds upon my proposal of 6, I will assess their feedback to determine whether to push further towards 8 or 9, or to explore negative values. If they reject or counter with a lower value, I will re-evaluate the group's preferences and adjust my strategy to maximize my utility, potentially by proposing a value like 0 or -2 to gauge their response to more significant changes.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "0e55f95a-ea5d-4373-895b-0805a14520cc"}, {"answer": "\nGiven momentum toward higher values, let's test stability by holding at <VALUE>6</VALUE>. If this draws broader support, we can reassess small upward steps next.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "0e55f95a-ea5d-4373-895b-0805a14520cc"}, {"answer": "\nThe jump from 2 to 6 bypasses significant testing ground; such leaps risk overlooking stable intermediate solutions. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "0e55f95a-ea5d-4373-895b-0805a14520cc"}, {"answer": "\nWe should avoid unnecessary risk and re-anchor at the cautious baseline already tested for stability. Stepping down now provides a safer reference point before any further exploration.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "0e55f95a-ea5d-4373-895b-0805a14520cc"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. We're tasked with selecting a single integer x within the shared range [-10, 10]. Let's begin with a neutral baseline to calibrate our perspectives.\n\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n\nI propose we start here and adjust incrementally based on everyone's input, seeking a stable solution that balances all our objectives.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "fde19efb-2293-4f17-84c6-104c7f55ec0a"}, {"answer": "\nStarting from 0, let's take a cautious step to the safer side to minimize unnecessary risk.\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\nWe can reassess at this level before considering any upward moves.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "fde19efb-2293-4f17-84c6-104c7f55ec0a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nI propose this adjustment to encourage more decisive movement and to better understand the group's preferences regarding larger magnitudes.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal and consider the possibility of moving further away from 0, either positively or negatively, depending on the group's responses and my ongoing assessment of their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "fde19efb-2293-4f17-84c6-104c7f55ec0a"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the exploration, but moving too far into negative territory raises concerns about system stability. Let me suggest we return to a more moderate position.\n\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "fde19efb-2293-4f17-84c6-104c7f55ec0a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "fde19efb-2293-4f17-84c6-104c7f55ec0a"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's return to zero suggests some convergence around this baseline. Let me propose a modest step forward to test if positive territory can work for the group.\n\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "fde19efb-2293-4f17-84c6-104c7f55ec0a"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s revert to a cautious baseline to minimize risk while we gauge comfort around zero.\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\nThis incremental move keeps us aligned while we learn more before any push upward.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "fde19efb-2293-4f17-84c6-104c7f55ec0a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nI propose this adjustment to encourage further exploration of the positive territory and gauge the group's comfort with slightly larger magnitudes.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal and consider the possibility of moving further into positive territory or reassessing the group's preferences regarding negative values, depending on the responses and my ongoing assessment of their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "fde19efb-2293-4f17-84c6-104c7f55ec0a"}, {"answer": "\nGiven emerging comfort around small positives, let's test a gentle step higher while staying cautious.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nThis incremental move should help us gauge tolerance for slightly higher positive territory.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "fde19efb-2293-4f17-84c6-104c7f55ec0a"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's move to 3 shows growing confidence in positive territory, but let me propose a slight pullback that may offer better stability for the full group.\n\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "fde19efb-2293-4f17-84c6-104c7f55ec0a"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk, let's take a small step back for stability. <VALUE>1</VALUE> keeps us cautious while still honoring recent interest in modest positives.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "fde19efb-2293-4f17-84c6-104c7f55ec0a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nI propose this adjustment to further explore the group's comfort with slightly larger positive magnitudes and to encourage more decisive moves.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal and consider moving further into positive territory if the group seems receptive, or reassessing the viability of negative values based on their responses and my ongoing analysis of their potential utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "fde19efb-2293-4f17-84c6-104c7f55ec0a"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious nudge upward should be safe to probe comfort while staying moderate.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nIf this draws resistance, we can stabilize at 3 next.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "fde19efb-2293-4f17-84c6-104c7f55ec0a"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious pullback avoids unnecessary risk and respects earlier support for low positives. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "fde19efb-2293-4f17-84c6-104c7f55ec0a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI propose this to further explore the group's comfort with slightly larger positive magnitudes.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal and consider moving further into positive territory if the group seems receptive, or propose a negative value to test the group's openness to alternative solutions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "fde19efb-2293-4f17-84c6-104c7f55ec0a"}, {"answer": "\nThe group shows tension between exploring higher positives and maintaining stability\u2014let me propose a middle ground that balances both camps' concerns.\n\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "fde19efb-2293-4f17-84c6-104c7f55ec0a"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Our shared constraint is clear: -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10.\n\nTo begin our exploration of the solution space, I propose we start from a neutral baseline and adjust incrementally based on everyone's input.\n\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n\nLet's hear from each party and work toward a stable, balanced solution.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "9bd32baa-831d-46f8-ba0b-ba4fb97a51d3"}, {"answer": "\nStarting from our baseline, I suggest we explore the low positive range, which often provides good system stability and balanced performance across multiple objectives.\n\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "9bd32baa-831d-46f8-ba0b-ba4fb97a51d3"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI suggest moving further in the positive direction to explore potential benefits of larger absolute values.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal and consider challenging the group to explore negative values if the discussion stagnates near small positive integers.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "9bd32baa-831d-46f8-ba0b-ba4fb97a51d3"}, {"answer": "\nStepping down keeps us within safe bounds and aligns with earlier low-positive preferences, minimizing unnecessary risk while staying within the allowed step. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "9bd32baa-831d-46f8-ba0b-ba4fb97a51d3"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's return to x = 2 suggests this region offers good cross-party stability. Before we settle, I'd like to hear Analyst A's perspective on this value\u2014their input will help us confirm we've found a robust solution.\n\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "9bd32baa-831d-46f8-ba0b-ba4fb97a51d3"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious one-step reduction helps avoid unnecessary risk while staying close to the region that already drew support.\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\nIf that proves too conservative, we can revert to the previous point to keep momentum.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "9bd32baa-831d-46f8-ba0b-ba4fb97a51d3"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nI propose moving towards a slightly larger positive value to continue exploring potential benefits while considering the group's tendency towards caution.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the group's reaction to this proposal, paying close attention to any pushback or support. If the group seems unwilling to move further in the positive direction, I may suggest exploring negative values to challenge our understanding of the solution space and inferred utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "9bd32baa-831d-46f8-ba0b-ba4fb97a51d3"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward move stays within the cautious positive region and close to the group\u2019s recent preferences. This remains incremental while checking if modestly higher still holds for everyone.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "9bd32baa-831d-46f8-ba0b-ba4fb97a51d3"}, {"answer": "\nA modest nudge upward tests if slightly higher remains comfortable for everyone. <VALUE>5</VALUE> If that draws pushback, we can step back while staying in the cautious positive range.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "9bd32baa-831d-46f8-ba0b-ba4fb97a51d3"}, {"answer": "\nWhile exploring upward is valuable, Delegate D's earlier pullback to x = 1 signals concern about climbing too high. Let me suggest a modest step back to better balance all perspectives.\n\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "9bd32baa-831d-46f8-ba0b-ba4fb97a51d3"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nI propose a moderate increase to continue exploring the potential benefits of larger positive values, while still being mindful of the group's cautious tendencies.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the group's reaction to this proposal, paying close attention to any pushback or support. If the group seems unwilling to move further in the positive direction, I may suggest exploring negative values, such as -4 or -5, to challenge our understanding of the solution space and inferred utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "9bd32baa-831d-46f8-ba0b-ba4fb97a51d3"}, {"answer": "\nA careful step back keeps us within safer bounds while remaining incremental.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nThis tests whether smaller positive values are more comfortable before we consider further adjustments.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "9bd32baa-831d-46f8-ba0b-ba4fb97a51d3"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down reduces risk while keeping us in a modest positive range.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nLet\u2019s test comfort here before considering a small fallback if needed.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "9bd32baa-831d-46f8-ba0b-ba4fb97a51d3"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's proposal of x = 2 offers a thoughtful balance between the upward exploration preferences and the signals that higher values may strain comfort zones. I support this position as a stable middle ground that respects all perspectives.\n\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "9bd32baa-831d-46f8-ba0b-ba4fb97a51d3"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>3</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "9bd32baa-831d-46f8-ba0b-ba4fb97a51d3"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nI propose this increase to continue exploring the group's comfort with moderate positive values and to challenge our understanding of the solution space, given the current stability around x = 3. This step aims to balance the need for incremental progress with the desire to test the group's willingness to adopt a slightly bolder stance.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "9bd32baa-831d-46f8-ba0b-ba4fb97a51d3"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, everyone. Our shared constraint is clear: we must choose an integer x within the range [-10, 10].\n\nTo establish a neutral baseline for our discussion, I propose we begin at <VALUE>0</VALUE>.\n\nFrom a systems architecture perspective, starting at the origin gives us room to explore in either direction as we learn each party's preferences and work toward a stable, balanced solution.\n\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "36d20654-5b03-448b-93bf-d95949aacc2d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\nA one-step move down from 0 is a prudent, low-risk probe that keeps us close to center while we learn everyone\u2019s preferences.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "36d20654-5b03-448b-93bf-d95949aacc2d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nThis move maintains the direction of Delegate D's proposal while encouraging a more decisive step away from the origin, allowing us to better understand each other's preferences.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions of Builder B and Delegate D to this proposal. If they resist moving further away from 0, I might infer that they have a strong preference for centrality or smaller absolute values. Alternatively, if they accommodate or even suggest larger steps, it could indicate that they are open to exploring more extreme values, which would help me refine my understanding of their utility functions and adjust my strategy accordingly.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "36d20654-5b03-448b-93bf-d95949aacc2d"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the quick move down, a small step back toward center is a cautious way to test tolerance without overcommitting.\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nThis keeps us near current preferences while checking if slightly higher remains acceptable.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "36d20654-5b03-448b-93bf-d95949aacc2d"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious one-step move upward keeps us close to the current cluster while testing comfort with slightly higher values.\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "36d20654-5b03-448b-93bf-d95949aacc2d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nA cautious one-step down balances differing preferences while avoiding unnecessary risk. Let\u2019s confirm this modest drop is acceptable before considering larger moves.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "36d20654-5b03-448b-93bf-d95949aacc2d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\nThis move encourages a more decisive step away from the origin, allowing us to better understand each other's preferences and potentially uncover more about the other parties' utility functions.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe how the other parties react to this proposal. If they resist this move, it could confirm their preference for centrality or smaller absolute values, guiding my next step. If they accommodate, it might suggest they are open to exploring more extreme values, which could help refine my understanding of their utility functions and inform my subsequent strategy.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "36d20654-5b03-448b-93bf-d95949aacc2d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n\nMoving back toward center provides better stability and robustness\u2014extreme values in either direction tend to introduce unnecessary risk into the system design.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "36d20654-5b03-448b-93bf-d95949aacc2d"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious one-step down reduces exposure while staying close to the current cluster.\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nThis tests comfort with slightly lower values without overcommitting.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "36d20654-5b03-448b-93bf-d95949aacc2d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n\nMoving back toward the center provides better system balance\u2014our recent drift into more negative territory increases design fragility, and a return to near-zero offers broader robustness.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "36d20654-5b03-448b-93bf-d95949aacc2d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nThis move slightly adjusts our current position to explore the group's comfort with negative values closer to what I previously suggested, aiming for a more decisive stance without overly disrupting the balance sought by other parties.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will closely observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Analyst A and Builder B, to gauge their flexibility regarding negative values. If this move is accepted, I may propose a further adjustment to explore the limits of the group's preference for negative values, potentially revealing more about their utility functions and guiding my strategy to maximize my own utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "36d20654-5b03-448b-93bf-d95949aacc2d"}, {"answer": "\nA small step up should keep us close to the current cluster while easing concerns about drifting too negative.\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "36d20654-5b03-448b-93bf-d95949aacc2d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\nThis proposal continues to encourage a more decisive step away from the origin, allowing us to better understand each other's preferences.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe how the group reacts to this proposal, particularly if they accommodate or resist this move, to refine my understanding of their utility functions and guide my subsequent strategy to maximize my own utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "36d20654-5b03-448b-93bf-d95949aacc2d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n\nThe recent drift to -4 introduces severe instability\u2014we need to return toward the center zone where system integrity is maintained and multiple design constraints can be satisfied simultaneously.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "36d20654-5b03-448b-93bf-d95949aacc2d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nA cautious step down tests comfort with slightly lower values while staying close to the current cluster. This avoids unnecessary risk while moving toward a safer bound for conservative preferences.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "36d20654-5b03-448b-93bf-d95949aacc2d"}, {"answer": "\nA small step up should keep us near the current cluster while easing concerns about drifting too negative. <VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "36d20654-5b03-448b-93bf-d95949aacc2d"}]}